! REPRODUCER, an ASSEMBLER finding already on the list as G3.1
! (docs/source_audit.md, "G3 -- Assembler completeness"), cut here
! because C22-6578 Chapter 4 prints it three times and says so itself.
! strap_asm.py refuses this deck:
!
!   cannot parse expression 'N*N-1.0' at '*N-1.0'
!
! The statement is C22-6578 printed p.42, Problem 4.8 (product of
! square matrices): "V-ICR,$3,N*N-1.0".  The page's comment (a):
! "STRAP I does not perform multiplication of addresses, but STRAP II
! will do it properly."  Printed p.40, Problem 4.6 Method 3, has
! "SF(BU,N*N,N), LOC" with the same remark: "The store field
! instruction will not be assembled correctly by STRAP I, because of
! the multiplication in the data description field.  STRAP II will do
! it properly."
!
! When it assembles with N = 8 the immediate must be 63.0 full words:
! the same half word as "V-ICR,$3,63.0".
! tests/check_problem_4_dd_refusals.py asserts the refusal.

N       SYN, 8
START   V-ICR,$3,N*N-1.0
        BEW, $
        END, START
